 ### Pre-marched Shadow and Ambient Occlusion Baking
-A technique to improve visual fidelity and performance by pre-calculating shadow and ambient occlusion data into the volume texture, leveraging the static nature of the cloud volume. It involves pre-marching a shadow ray through the volume (e.g., 4 shadow samples per cloud sample) and pre-marching ambient occlusion into the volume texture. This allows dynamic time-of-day changes and runtime shadow lookup with a single 3D texture lookup, matching the cloud geometry perfectly [S3, unofficial].
